# Q: can a map author set the exact composition and position of buildings and units?
# Q: does an exact force replace the generated base and formation rather than add to them?
#
#   MiVic.Game.exe --probe tools/probe/exact-force.probe --probe-out artifacts/probe/exact-force.txt
#
# The authoring half of the map format. `editor exact on` makes the placements the whole force,
# `editor place` and `editor unit` name a role and a spot, and `editor force` holds the two
# invariants that make the mode mean something: that what was placed is what stands, and that
# the force is one the file loader would take.
#
# The coordinates are the sites the generator picks for this seed — read off `base-ground.probe`
# and the editor's own structures — because an authored headquarters still has to stand on
# ground a headquarters can be founded on. A generated base occupies that ground while the mode
# is off, which is why `exact on` comes before the first placement.

editor report

# The generated world, before anything is authored: the mission's own layout, and no force
# problems, because there is nothing authored to have a problem with.
editor force

# Exact first, then place: in generated mode the generator's own headquarters stands on the
# ground an authored one would be founded on.
editor exact on

editor tool structure
editor place CommandCentre -248.4 -117.2 0
editor place CommandCentre 145.3 -98.5 1
editor place CommandCentre -4.7 192.1 2

editor tool unit
editor unit Tank -240 -117 0
editor unit Tank -240 -110 0
editor unit Infantry -235 -117 0

# Six placements, six entities standing: no generated base, no generated formation, and a force
# the loader would take.
editor force
editor report

editor name probe-exact-force
editor save
editor report
